    <div class="tab-pane" id="guide-rest">
      <h4 class="phpclaw-section-title">REST API</h4>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">
        Integrate phpClaw into any frontend, mobile app, or external service via Magento's standard Web API.
        All routes follow Magento REST conventions and return Magento's standard response and error envelopes.
      </p>

      <h3>Authentication</h3>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">Every request needs an admin bearer token. Obtain one with:</p>
      <pre class="phpclaw-pre">POST /rest/V1/integration/admin/token
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"admin","password":"&lt;your-password&gt;"}</pre>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">Pass the returned token on subsequent calls: <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code></p>

      <h3 class="phpclaw-mt-24">Routes</h3>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">phpClaw exposes exactly two routes. Both sit on <code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code>, so any admin role holding that resource can call them, and both are scoped to the caller's own conversations unless the caller also holds <code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_settings</code>.</p>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="phpclaw-th-endpoint">Method &amp; URL</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th class="phpclaw-th-name">ACL resource</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Agent</strong></td></tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>POST /rest/V1/phpclaw/send</code></td>
            <td>Run the agent synchronously with a free-form prompt.</td>
            <td><code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>POST /rest/V1/phpclaw/chat/stream</code></td>
            <td>Server-Sent Events stream: same agent run but emits frames as the agent progresses.</td>
            <td><code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3 class="phpclaw-mt-24">POST <code>/rest/V1/phpclaw/send</code></h3>
      <pre class="phpclaw-pre">{
  "message": "low stock products"
}

Response (200):
{
  "text": "Here are the low-stock products...",
  "provider": "anthropic",
  "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
  "tokens": 783,
  "iterations": 2
}</pre>

      <h3 class="phpclaw-mt-24">Error responses</h3>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">All errors use Magento's standard envelope: <code>{"message": "...", "parameters": {...}}</code>. Status codes:</p>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="phpclaw-th-status-sm">Status</th>
            <th>When</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>400</td><td>Empty <code>message</code> field, a Magento <code>InputException</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>401</td><td>Missing or invalid bearer token, or a token whose role lacks <code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code>. Magento refuses both with 401 and names the required resource in <code>parameters</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>403</td><td>The conversation belongs to another admin user</td></tr>
          <tr><td>422</td><td>Guard blocked the message: prompt injection or PII detected</td></tr>
          <tr><td>500</td><td>Provider or tool error: see <code>message</code> for details</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3 class="phpclaw-mt-24">curl example</h3>
      <pre class="phpclaw-pre">TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"username":"admin","password":"&lt;pass&gt;"}' \
  https://example.com/rest/V1/integration/admin/token | tr -d '"')

curl -X POST https://example.com/rest/V1/phpclaw/send \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"message":"low stock products"}'</pre>

      <h3 class="phpclaw-mt-24">Streaming Endpoint (Server-Sent Events)</h3>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">
        phpClaw exposes two SSE endpoints that emit live tool activity and the final assistant payload.
        Use them for chat surfaces that want a real-time experience similar to the built-in admin chat.
      </p>

      <h4>Admin endpoint: session-authed, powers the built-in Chat page</h4>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th class="phpclaw-th-endpoint">URL</th><td><code>POST /admin/phpclaw/chat/stream</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Auth</th><td>Admin session + Magento <code>form_key</code> (CSRF)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>ACL</th><td><code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Body</th><td><code>{"message":"…","conversation_id":"…","form_key":"…"}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Response</th><td><code>text/event-stream</code> with <code>X-Accel-Buffering: no</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h4 class="phpclaw-mt-16">REST endpoint: bearer-token authed, for external clients</h4>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th class="phpclaw-th-endpoint">URL</th><td><code>POST /rest/V1/phpclaw/chat/stream</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Auth</th><td>Admin bearer token (obtain via <code>POST /rest/V1/integration/admin/token</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>ACL</th><td><code>PhpClaw_Magento::phpclaw_chat</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Body</th><td><code>{"message":"…","conversationId":"…"}</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Response</th><td><code>text/event-stream</code>, where frames are <code>event:</code> + <code>data:</code> lines separated by <code>\n\n</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h4 class="phpclaw-mt-16">Event types</h4>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="phpclaw-th-endpoint">Event</th>
            <th>Payload</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>tool_before</code></td><td>A tool is about to execute. Render a placeholder card with the tool name and inputs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>tool_after</code></td><td>A tool returned. Replace the placeholder with the typed result card.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>chunk</code></td><td><code>{"text":"&lt;token&gt;"}</code>, incremental assistant tokens. Accumulate into the live assistant bubble.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>done</code></td><td><code>text, provider, model, tokens, iterations, conversation_id, title, is_new, tool_calls, run_id</code>, the final summary.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>error</code></td><td>Guard blocked or provider failed. Includes <code>error</code> and HTTP <code>code</code> (422 / 502 / 504 / 500).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h4 class="phpclaw-mt-16">Sample event stream</h4>
      <pre class="phpclaw-pre">event: tool_before
data: {"tool_name":"magento_products","tool_input":{"limit":2}}

event: tool_after
data: {"tool_name":"magento_products","tool_input":{"limit":2},"tool_result":"[{\"sku\":\"PHC-010\"}, ...]"}

event: done
data: {"text":"Here are 2 products...","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen2.5:7b","tokens":1312,"iterations":2,"conversation_id":"01KSJ...","tool_calls":[...]}</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-pane" id="guide-cli">
      <h4 class="phpclaw-section-title">CLI Commands</h4>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">Run from your Magento project root. All settings are read from <em>phpClaw &rarr; Settings</em>; the CLI honours whatever is saved there.</p>

      <h3>Agent</h3>
      <table class="phpclaw-table">
