    <div class="tab-pane" id="guide-privacy">
      <h4 class="phpclaw-section-title">Privacy &amp; Data Storage</h4>
      <p class="phpclaw-body-text">
        The <strong>Store Messages</strong> setting in
        <?= $block->settingsLink() ?> <span class="phpclaw-text-muted">(Administrator only)</span>
        controls what data phpClaw persists. All data stays on your server, and nothing is shared externally unless you enable cloud forwarding.
      </p>

      <table class="phpclaw-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th></th>
            <th>Store Messages = <span class="phpclaw-status-available">ON</span> (default)</th>
            <th>Store Messages = <span class="phpclaw-status-off">OFF</span></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Conversation metadata</strong><br><small>ID, title, timestamps</small></td>
            <td>&#10003; Saved to <code>phpclaw_conversations</code></td>
            <td>&#10007; <strong>Never saved</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Message text</strong><br><small>User prompts and AI replies</small></td>
            <td>&#10003; Saved to <code>phpclaw_messages</code></td>
            <td>&#10007; <strong>Never saved</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Tool call inputs/outputs</strong><br><small>Data returned by tools</small></td>
            <td>&#10003; Saved to <code>phpclaw_messages</code></td>
            <td>&#10007; <strong>Never saved</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="phpclaw-tip">
        <strong>Note:</strong> When <em>Store Messages</em> is OFF, multi-turn conversations still work within a single request, since the agent holds context in memory, but nothing is persisted. Each new request starts fresh.
      </div>

      <div class="phpclaw-tip phpclaw-mt-16">
        <strong>phpClaw Cloud:</strong> Request data (prompts, responses, tool calls, and metadata) is sent to phpClaw Cloud only when a Cloud Key is set <em>and</em> Store Messages is ON. When Store Messages is OFF, nothing is sent to the cloud. No data is shared with third parties.
      </div>

    </div>

